WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.097 --> 00:00:38.360
- Dre, you're ready?
- Yeah, one second.

2
00:00:39.422 --> 00:00:44.572
Oh Dre, I am so excited!
It's like we are brave pioneers,

3
00:00:44.672 --> 00:00:49.366
on a quest to start a new life
in a magical, new land.

4
00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:53.157
You could say that.

5
00:00:58.504 --> 00:01:00.980
Okay, all right, let's go.

6
00:01:05.258 --> 00:01:08.285
- And don't forget to use the bathroom.
- Okay. 

7
00:01:19.361 --> 00:01:22.842
Be careful with that guys, okay?

8
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.758
- I'll see you later, uncle Charlie.
- C'mon Dre, we can't miss this plane!

9
00:01:31.984 --> 00:01:36.208
Bye guys!
We're gonna miss you.

10
00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.773
- No man, it's yours.
- C'mon Dre, just take it.

11
00:01:47.294 --> 00:01:50.460
Thanks, man!

12
00:01:53.085 --> 00:01:55.843
Okay Dre, c'mon, we have to go.
Okay, bye guys!

13
00:01:55.885 --> 00:01:57.843
We'll call you as soon as we land.

14
00:02:54.736 --> 00:02:58.994
<i>- Ladies and gentlemen, welcome to flight CA982.
- You got it? - Yeah.</i>

15
00:02:58.995 --> 00:03:03.756
<i>- With our service to Beijing.</i>
- Oh Dre look, we are already on lesson ten.

16
00:03:04.385 --> 00:03:07.294
How are you?

17
00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:14.466
- Remember what that one is?
- No.

18
00:03:15.095 --> 00:03:17.099
Dre, you're killing me.

19
00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:23.074
Mom, look, in China everything is old.
There's old houses, old parks...

20
00:03:23.174 --> 00:03:28.767
old people...Look, this guy is at least
four-hundred years old.

21
00:03:28.913 --> 00:03:31.407
Dre, please focus.
Okay?

22
00:03:34.312 --> 00:03:37.614
What's your name?

23
00:03:37.743 --> 00:03:39.573
You need to practice.
Yeah, you need to try.

24
00:03:39.743 --> 00:03:40.573
No, mom.

25
00:03:40.613 --> 00:03:43.129
- Yes, Dre. Dre...
- Mom?

26
00:03:43.837 --> 00:03:47.081
- Ask him. Go ahead.
- No, mom.

27
00:03:47.082 --> 00:03:50.755
Ask him "what's your name"
and "how are you". Do it, now.

28
00:04:03.806 --> 00:04:07.383
Dude, I'm from Detroit.

29
00:04:13.064 --> 00:04:15.737
What's up?

30
00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:27.408
It's said to meet her
at number five.

31
00:05:30.074 --> 00:05:32.410
Mrs. Packer?

32
00:05:34.002 --> 00:05:40.489
- Hi. It's Parker.
- Oh, apologies, Mrs. Parker. Welcome to Beijing.

33
00:06:03.694 --> 00:06:07.418
Look! There is Omatek village.
Isn't it beautiful?

34
00:06:08.953 --> 00:06:12.655
Yes. I guess there's nothing
old in China, huh Dre?

35
00:06:33.829 --> 00:06:36.010
Look at that, Dre. Beverly Hills.

36
00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.632
We've always talked about
living there, huh?

37
00:06:38.732 --> 00:06:41.207
I think we have talked
about the other one, mom.

38
00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:44.493
I got a good feeling about this.

39
00:06:50.361 --> 00:06:53.339
Oh, yeah. You must be the new
dude in 305. I'm Harry.

40
00:06:53.439 --> 00:06:56.209
- Hey, what's up? I'm Dre.
- Here. Let me help you.

41
00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.547
Thanks, man.

42
00:06:59.466 --> 00:07:02.263
- Welcome to the building, Dre.
- Thanks.

43
00:07:03.412 --> 00:07:09.147
Can you please explain this electricity card,
because we-we don't have these in America.

44
00:07:13.043 --> 00:07:17.153
- Know any Chinese?
- Nah.

45
00:07:17.787 --> 00:07:20.899
This is China.
Might not be a bad idea.

46
00:07:23.161 --> 00:07:26.049
Oh, that's our park.
You should come.

47
00:07:26.084 --> 00:07:29.583
Look at you.
Making friends already.

48
00:07:30.293 --> 00:07:32.423
- Hi, I'm Dre's mother.
- Nice to meet you.

49
00:07:32.523 --> 00:07:34.616
Nice to meet you too.
You can call me Miss Sherry.

50
00:07:34.716 --> 00:07:36.709
- I'm Harry.
- Hi, Harry.

51
00:07:37.744 --> 00:07:40.112
- So, I guess, I'll see you later, then?
- Maybe.

52
00:07:40.144 --> 00:07:42.412
Okay, cool. See you.

53
00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.409
Ok, this is your rental agreement in English.

54
00:07:54.509 --> 00:07:58.971
So the landlady is Mrs. Wong.
Her English is not good.

55
00:07:59.728 --> 00:08:02.419
But if something goes wrong,
you go to Mr. Han.

56
00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.819
- His English is very good.
- Okay.

57
00:08:04.501 --> 00:08:08.371
Okay. So, welcome to Beijing, Mrs. Parker.
Um, so I see you tomorrow, okay?

58
00:08:08.471 --> 00:08:11.982
Okay, sure! Thank you.
Oh, wait, wait!

59
00:08:12.371 --> 00:08:14.982
<i>Um, you mentioned something
about going...</i>

60
00:08:27.027 --> 00:08:30.926
Oh, this is perfect, Dre. Everything we
need is in walking distance.

61
00:08:31.026 --> 00:08:33.034
Oh, you know what,
we can have lunch together

62
00:08:33.035 --> 00:08:34.934
every day at your school,
if you wanted to.

63
00:08:35.034 --> 00:08:37.267
Negative! Not a chance.

64
00:08:40.769 --> 00:08:44.872
Dre, we are not doing this in Beijing.

65
00:08:46.746 --> 00:08:49.051
Dre, pick up your jacket!

66
00:08:49.151 --> 00:08:52.537
Mom, I'm tired, okay?
I have airplane lag.

67
00:08:57.328 --> 00:09:00.015
Airplane...

68
00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:04.149
It's jet lag.

69
00:09:04.249 --> 00:09:07.747
I know baby, I got it too.

70
00:09:09.814 --> 00:09:15.513
But, we can't go to sleep. Cause then we'll
be up at 2 A.M. You have school tomorrow.

71
00:09:25.843 --> 00:09:30.076
<i>Dre, can you please go
find the maintenance man?!</i>

72
00:09:30.176 --> 00:09:32.845
<i>I need to take a shower,
and the hot water is broken!</i>

73
00:09:32.846 --> 00:09:33.545
Yes.

74
00:09:35.227 --> 00:09:37.769
Excuse me.

75
00:09:37.927 --> 00:09:41.723
Um, the maintenance man?
Mr. Han?

76
00:09:44.756 --> 00:09:47.372
Thanks.

77
00:09:59.659 --> 00:10:02.148
Mr. Han?

78
00:10:02.248 --> 00:10:07.835
Me and my mom, we just moved in. 305.
The hot water is not working.

79
00:10:10.055 --> 00:10:13.328
Mr. Han?

80
00:10:17.371 --> 00:10:22.336
Okay. Alright I just come back another time.

81
00:10:22.835 --> 00:10:26.682
Or you can just show me how to do it so,
I can get out of your hair.

82
00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.715
Um, I can always come back
if this is bad time.

83
00:11:34.744 --> 00:11:37.163
- Hey man, you made it. Welcome.
- Thanks.

84
00:11:37.718 --> 00:11:39.898
- You play, right? C'mon.
- Yeah.

85
00:11:44.654 --> 00:11:47.344
- Us three against them four.
- All right.

86
00:11:58.654 --> 00:11:59.944
Pass!

87
00:12:06.354 --> 00:12:08.944
What's up?
What's up?

88
00:12:09.613 --> 00:12:13.043
My shooting hand.
Got some jet lag so...

89
00:12:13.313 --> 00:12:15.043
You know, I'm just...

90
00:12:29.978 --> 00:12:32.821
You want this?

91
00:12:32.921 --> 00:12:37.156
You want me to play? You know
I have no problem beatin' old people.

92
00:12:41.084 --> 00:12:44.083
Back where I come from they call me
"Ping Pong Dre", alright?

93
00:12:44.084 --> 00:12:46.083
I'm going to take it easy on you.

94
00:13:14.919 --> 00:13:18.413
Come on, man.
I'm twelve.

95
00:13:27.075 --> 00:13:29.975
He is really good.
I've never seen him lose to anybody.

96
00:13:30.775 --> 00:13:31.975
Yeah.

97
00:13:34.868 --> 00:13:38.892
- Dude. You're gonna talk to her or what?
- To who?

98
00:13:38.992 --> 00:13:43.129
- To her. The girl you've been staring at.
- I wasn't staring at her, dude.

99
00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:45.525
Yeah, you were.

100
00:13:46.943 --> 00:13:51.709
- You should go talk to her, unless you're scared?
- I'm not scared of anything.

101
00:13:51.809 --> 00:13:54.334
Then do it. Go.
Come on.

102
00:13:56.364 --> 00:13:59.470
Right now.

103
00:14:04.416 --> 00:14:08.238
Hey, what's up?

104
00:14:10.772 --> 00:14:14.752
I forgot.
No English, um...

105
00:14:21.952 --> 00:14:25.725
What language was that?

106
00:14:25.825 --> 00:14:28.686
You speak English?
Me too.

107
00:14:29.834 --> 00:14:34.047
- So, what are you listening to?
- Bach.

108
00:14:34.147 --> 00:14:39.407
Bach, I listen to them all the time.
They are tight. Have you ever heard of this?

109
00:14:46.358 --> 00:14:48.898
Oh yeah, you like it huh, right?!

110
00:15:01.723 --> 00:15:05.886
Great move, one over here.

111
00:15:06.809 --> 00:15:10.780
- Wait, wait it's coming back.
- May I touch your hair?

112
00:15:13.289 --> 00:15:15.673
You want to touch my hair?

113
00:15:18.421 --> 00:15:21.056
Um...Sure.

114
00:15:31.717 --> 00:15:34.397
You shoud be practicing.

115
00:15:34.497 --> 00:15:36.182
I'm practicing.

116
00:15:36.197 --> 00:15:38.564
- What you're doing, you won't be needing these.
- What's your problem?

117
00:15:38.664 --> 00:15:40.385
Leave it.

118
00:15:47.711 --> 00:15:49.270
Come on, dude.

119
00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.962
I said, leave it.

120
00:16:17.273 --> 00:16:19.607
You want to fight?

121
00:16:38.693 --> 00:16:40.987
- Are you okay?
- Leave me alone.

122
00:16:41.087 --> 00:16:43.663
I'm fine.

123
00:16:45.414 --> 00:16:49.315
- Dre, dude...
- Leave me alone.

124
00:17:27.762 --> 00:17:32.139
Dre, are you ready?
Cause we got to be there in like 20 minutes.

125
00:17:32.239 --> 00:17:34.363
I know, mom.

126
00:17:34.463 --> 00:17:36.931
- And you have your uniform on, right?
- Yes, mom.

127
00:17:37.031 --> 00:17:39.561
Don't break any rules
on the first day.

128
00:17:41.221 --> 00:17:44.560
Okay, come on, I'm waiting for you.

129
00:17:53.212 --> 00:17:55.830
Wait, you don't have to comin', I mean...
I can handle it.

130
00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:58.191
Dre, don't be silly, it's your first day.

131
00:17:58.192 --> 00:18:01.305
Plus, we both have to meet the
assist principal Mrs. Pong.

132
00:18:01.405 --> 00:18:04.641
I can find her.
You need to get to work, right?!

133
00:18:04.741 --> 00:18:07.124
- Are you trying to get rid of me?
- No, mom.

134
00:18:09.101 --> 00:18:12.067
Mrs. Pong.
Hi, Mrs. Pong.

135
00:18:12.167 --> 00:18:15.482
- Mrs. Parker,  we've been waiting.
- I'm so sorry we are late...

136
00:18:15.483 --> 00:18:17.279
We just flew from Detroit last night...

137
00:18:17.379 --> 00:18:20.040
- And this is my son Dre.
- Hello.

138
00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:25.238
- We only wear uniforms on Uniform day.
- Oh, that's my fault.

139
00:18:25.338 --> 00:18:30.059
I didn't have a chance to read the school packages
sent to me. Will be better tomorrow.

140
00:18:30.686 --> 00:18:36.908
- And hats are not permitted.
- Yeah, I should've read up on the dress code.

141
00:18:37.008 --> 00:18:41.882
- Dre, is that make-up? What is that?
- Mom, I ran into a pole.

142
00:18:41.982 --> 00:18:46.887
- No, you have a black eye. You've got into a fight?
- Fighting is not tolerated here.

143
00:18:46.987 --> 00:18:50.390
You heard him, he ran into a pole.
Come here, Dre.

144
00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:52.342
- Mom, don't start.
- Who did it?

145
00:18:52.442 --> 00:18:55.479
Nobody mom, I ran into a pole. I ain't tell
you cause I know you would react like this.

146
00:18:55.579 --> 00:18:58.494
Dre, you know I don't play,
if somebody hit my baby, I would tear...

147
00:18:58.579 --> 00:19:01.494
I know mom,
that's why I don't tell you stuff.

148
00:19:01.594 --> 00:19:04.637
- Just relax, I just ran into a...
- Yeah, yeah,  you ran into a pole.

149
00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:14.494
Alright Dre, alright, alright. Look, go to class,
go to  class, but we will talk about this later.

150
00:19:15.023 --> 00:19:17.725
Okay? Alright, go!

151
00:19:19.802 --> 00:19:22.763
- I love you.
- Mom?!

152
00:19:23.372 --> 00:19:26.447
I said I love you.

153
00:19:26.547 --> 00:19:30.056
- Okay, I love you too.
- Okay, have a good day.

154
00:19:47.047 --> 00:19:49.756
- Hi.
- Hey!

155
00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:01.145
You know,
we only wear uniforms on Uniform day.

156
00:20:01.775 --> 00:20:05.913
Oh yeah, I still got that one.

157
00:20:09.032 --> 00:20:11.730
Thanks.

158
00:20:12.433 --> 00:20:15.665
- I'm Meiying.
- I'm Dre.

159
00:20:23.221 --> 00:20:25.807
Sorry about Cheng.

160
00:20:25.907 --> 00:20:28.980
So that's his name?!

161
00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.342
- Is he your boyfriend?
- No.

162
00:20:32.442 --> 00:20:36.954
- Our parents are very close.
- He definitely likes you.

163
00:20:37.627 --> 00:20:41.572
- I have to go practice.
- Wait...

164
00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:45.767
- You eat and practice at the same time?
- Yes.

165
00:20:45.867 --> 00:20:50.819
But, my mom says if you eat standing up,
it gives you gas.

166
00:20:50.919 --> 00:20:53.875
You're funny.

167
00:21:32.873 --> 00:21:35.733
- Come to fix the hot water.
- It's in there.

168
00:22:02.167 --> 00:22:04.623
Kid?
Kid?!

169
00:22:20.227 --> 00:22:24.804
Did you just hit me in my neck
with a toothpaste cap?!

170
00:22:25.785 --> 00:22:28.274
Hot water fine.
Flip switch.

171
00:22:28.374 --> 00:22:32.770
Wait half hour, take shower,
flip switch off.

172
00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:35.343
Why don't you just leave it on?

173
00:22:35.443 --> 00:22:39.090
- You leave on in America?
- We don't have a switch in America.

174
00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:42.138
Get switch,
Save planet.

175
00:22:43.719 --> 00:22:47.617
- What happened to your eye?
- I ran into a pole.

176
00:22:48.841 --> 00:22:51.392
Interesting pole.

177
00:22:51.812 --> 00:22:55.257
- Dre?! I'm back.
- That's my mom.</i>

178
00:22:55.357 --> 00:22:57.148
End it, do the handle, it's messed up.

179
00:22:57.248 --> 00:22:59.538
<i>- Are you ready for school?
- Yeah.</i>

180
00:23:02.244 --> 00:23:05.851
- Hey, let me help you.
- They have your favorite cereal here, I found it.

181
00:23:13.587 --> 00:23:19.912
Dre, for the one hundredth time,
can you please pick up your jacket?

182
00:23:20.012 --> 00:23:23.725
- One second, mom.
- No! Not in one second, now!

183
00:23:24.298 --> 00:23:25.741
This programme is about to be over.
Give me two minutes.

184
00:23:25.742 --> 00:23:28.741
Dre, I don't care!
Come and pick it up now.

185
00:23:28.841 --> 00:23:32.433
- God, how many times do I have to ask you?
- Once.

186
00:23:32.533 --> 00:23:35.218
- That's right. Make it happen.
- "What's with you and the jacket?!"

187
00:23:35.318 --> 00:23:36.946
- I'm sorry, what was that?
- Nothing.

188
00:23:37.046 --> 00:23:39.109
Okay, just what I thought...
Nothing.

189
00:23:40.501 --> 00:23:42.815
Thank you.

190
00:25:02.529 --> 00:25:05.705
From the top again.

191
00:25:29.783 --> 00:25:37.229
Okay. It's enough please. You are rushing it.
You must play the pauses.

192
00:25:37.664 --> 00:25:42.925
Do you know how important this is for your family?
What it will mean for your life?

193
00:25:43.589 --> 00:25:46.513
We have to work this weekend.
I'm calling you father.

194
00:25:51.919 --> 00:25:54.018
We continue.

195
00:26:04.656 --> 00:26:07.479
- How that sound?
- Almost like a Chinese.

196
00:26:07.579 --> 00:26:12.545
Yeah, I'm fluent. And I don't know about that guy
was talking about? I thought you sounded great.

197
00:26:12.645 --> 00:26:14.865
Thank you.

198
00:26:22.370 --> 00:26:30.484
- So, you are practicing for anything? Like a show?
- Yes, I have an audition next month...

199
00:26:30.584 --> 00:26:37.216
- For the Beijing Academy of Music.
- Beijing Academy of Music. Sounds important.

200
00:26:37.393 --> 00:26:43.511
You know, their initials spell BAM.

201
00:26:47.318 --> 00:26:49.340
What?

202
00:26:51.545 --> 00:26:53.808
I gotta go.

203
00:27:15.962 --> 00:27:18.384
Can I touch your hair?

204
00:27:24.698 --> 00:27:26.952
You're gonna do something?

205
00:27:28.959 --> 00:27:31.610
Just stay away from us.

206
00:27:31.710 --> 00:27:35.342
All of us.

207
00:27:55.252 --> 00:27:57.284
Baby?!

208
00:27:59.012 --> 00:28:01.953
Dre, are you sleeping?

209
00:28:32.799 --> 00:28:36.399
- Um, can you sign this?
- For the Forbidden City?!

210
00:28:36.499 --> 00:28:40.958
I think it's funny that you have to give
my permission to go to the Forbidden City.

211
00:28:41.635 --> 00:28:45.158
- Pole in Beijing.
- Not funny, mom.

212
00:28:45.258 --> 00:28:47.381
Oh, cut it out, grumpy.

213
00:28:47.481 --> 00:28:50.329
I'm serious, Dre. This ice cream,
I don't know what they do it,

214
00:28:50.330 --> 00:28:53.329
but it's more flavoristic. What?

215
00:28:53.429 --> 00:28:58.653
Mom, this is you. "Oh my Godness, this ice cream
here is so good, and everything in China...

216
00:28:58.753 --> 00:29:01.680
is so much better than everything else..."
Aw, mom c'mon...

217
00:29:01.748 --> 00:29:05.511
First of all, I don't sound like that,
and I don't move all like that.

218
00:29:07.213 --> 00:29:09.589
You should get some ice cream, sweetie.

219
00:29:09.723 --> 00:29:12.941
- Mom, mom,  c'mon.
- Dre! Wait!

220
00:29:13.801 --> 00:29:16.799
Boy, you won't get running from me?!

221
00:29:20.254 --> 00:29:22.177
Kung Fu.

222
00:30:06.329 --> 00:30:07.917
What do we learn here?

223
00:30:08.017 --> 00:30:11.420
No weakness! No pain! No mercy!

224
00:30:19.849 --> 00:30:21.716
Begin!

225
00:30:29.616 --> 00:30:32.244
- Mom, mom, c'mon, let's go. C'mon, mom!
- What? Dre, we just got here.

226
00:30:33.524 --> 00:30:37.369
- Dre, what's going on?
- Nothing.

227
00:30:37.881 --> 00:30:40.868
- Dre, what happened?
- Nothing happened.

228
00:30:41.167 --> 00:30:45.150
What is it, you don't want to take that class?
Whatever Dre, What happened?

229
00:30:45.555 --> 00:30:50.286
We moved to China!
That's what happened!

230
00:31:04.529 --> 00:31:06.404
Okay, stop.

231
00:31:08.440 --> 00:31:11.412
Don't be like that, Dre.

232
00:31:13.428 --> 00:31:15.594
What do you want me to do?

233
00:31:15.694 --> 00:31:18.366
- We've been here less than a week...
- I feel like it's a year!

234
00:31:19.868 --> 00:31:22.492
I hate it here.

235
00:31:26.789 --> 00:31:29.640
Dre, please let me help you.

236
00:31:31.208 --> 00:31:34.251
I can't help you if you don't tell
me what's wrong?! Oh, please.

237
00:31:35.020 --> 00:31:37.065
You don't care what's wrong!

238
00:31:37.165 --> 00:31:40.702
All you care about is how happy I am
and how great ice cream is.

239
00:31:40.802 --> 00:31:45.254
I'm not happy.
I hate it here!

240
00:31:54.892 --> 00:31:57.611
I want to go home!

241
00:31:57.711 --> 00:32:04.299
Dre, we can't go home. Okay?
There is nothing left for us in Detroit.

242
00:32:04.399 --> 00:32:07.472
This is what we've got.

243
00:32:08.676 --> 00:32:11.996
This is home.

244
00:32:37.827 --> 00:32:39.651
<i>Gather on here.</i>

245
00:32:39.652 --> 00:32:43.444
<i>Welcome to one of the most popular
landmarks in all over China.</i>

246
00:32:43.445 --> 00:32:46.531
<i>It is visited by millions of people
every year.</i>

247
00:32:46.631 --> 00:32:49.676
<i>The Forbidden City.</i>

248
00:33:27.691 --> 00:33:29.835
You plaster on for good luck.

249
00:33:48.869 --> 00:33:52.786
- I wish someone would just...
- Yeah, me too.

250
00:33:54.450 --> 00:33:57.783
- Just tell someone.
- Yeah, I got it.

251
00:33:58.056 --> 00:34:00.410
Thanks a lot.

252
00:34:09.083 --> 00:34:13.722
<i>The walls of the palace were reinforced
with the bricks, 15 layers deep,</i>

253
00:34:13.723 --> 00:34:16.954
<i>to prevent anyone
from coming in.</i>

254
00:34:21.282 --> 00:34:24.598
- Mr. Parker... Is everything okay?
- Oh yes?

255
00:34:26.880 --> 00:34:30.455
Um...Yes, thank you.

256
00:36:34.169 --> 00:36:36.524
Get him.

257
00:36:41.090 --> 00:36:42.854
Come on.

258
00:38:21.450 --> 00:38:23.658
You're fast.

259
00:38:25.410 --> 00:38:28.108
But not fast enough.

260
00:38:44.376 --> 00:38:46.776
He's had enough.

261
00:38:46.863 --> 00:38:48.110
Don't you remember what we learned?

262
00:38:48.299 --> 00:38:49.111
No weakness. No pain.

263
00:38:52.292 --> 00:38:53.737
No mercy!

264
00:40:57.897 --> 00:41:00.981
Go home.

265
00:41:23.441 --> 00:41:26.213
- What's up with the light bulbs, Mr. Han?
- Shh!

266
00:42:04.467 --> 00:42:06.957
I thought you are just a maintenance man?

267
00:42:07.057 --> 00:42:10.648
You've seen only with your eyes,
so you are easy to fool.

268
00:42:13.685 --> 00:42:15.715
It doesn't hurt.

269
00:42:15.815 --> 00:42:18.246
Chauva.
Ancient Chinese healing.

270
00:42:18.890 --> 00:42:24.380
How did you do that up there? You like even
didn't punch them. They...beat each other up.

271
00:42:24.480 --> 00:42:26.833
When fighting angry, blind men...

272
00:42:26.933 --> 00:42:29.963
best we just stay out of the way.

273
00:42:32.675 --> 00:42:35.880
- So, where did you learn Kung Fu?
- From father.

274
00:42:36.467 --> 00:42:38.630
Have you ever taught anybody?

275
00:42:39.165 --> 00:42:41.583
No.

276
00:42:42.147 --> 00:42:44.781
Would you?

277
00:42:45.299 --> 00:42:47.878
- Depends.
- On what?

278
00:42:47.899 --> 00:42:51.878
- Reason.
- What about to kick somebody's ass?

279
00:42:55.343 --> 00:42:58.204
The best fights are the ones we avoid.

280
00:42:58.716 --> 00:43:01.061
What if I wanna avoid getting
my ass kicked?

281
00:43:01.161 --> 00:43:03.221
- Stop saying "ass".
- Sorry.

282
00:43:09.217 --> 00:43:11.763
Kung Fu is for knowledge, defense.

283
00:43:11.863 --> 00:43:14.946
Not to make war,
but to create peace.

284
00:43:15.092 --> 00:43:17.081
That's not definitely what they're taught.

285
00:43:17.785 --> 00:43:21.788
No such thing as bad student,
only bad teacher.

286
00:43:22.014 --> 00:43:27.098
That's great. I guess we'll just stroll in
their school and talk to their teacher.

287
00:43:27.985 --> 00:43:30.171
- Good idea.
- No, bad idea.

288
00:43:30.271 --> 00:43:32.527
If I go in there, I get my ass kick...

289
00:43:35.284 --> 00:43:38.819
- I'll get beat up.
- You got beat up anyway.

290
00:43:43.670 --> 00:43:46.410
Would you go with me?

291
00:43:47.198 --> 00:43:49.970
No, sorry.

292
00:43:50.876 --> 00:43:54.259
- But you said it was a good idea.
- For you, bad idea for me.

293
00:43:54.359 --> 00:43:58.080
C'mon, it's not like you should be busy
or anything...I don't even speak Chinese.

294
00:43:58.964 --> 00:44:01.216
Very sorry.

295
00:44:06.411 --> 00:44:10.717
Okay...Whatever.

296
00:44:25.914 --> 00:44:28.430
Wait!

297
00:45:07.222 --> 00:45:11.403
What are you doing?
Why did you stop?

298
00:45:12.341 --> 00:45:15.226
Finish!

299
00:45:18.870 --> 00:45:21.726
Okay, Mr. Han, let's get out of here.

300
00:45:25.690 --> 00:45:28.895
We do not stop when our enemy is down!

301
00:45:29.590 --> 00:45:31.159
No mercy.

302
00:45:31.259 --> 00:45:33.179
No mercy in the studio.

303
00:45:33.279 --> 00:45:36.044
No mercy in life.

304
00:45:40.859 --> 00:45:43.221
What are you looking at?

305
00:45:43.321 --> 00:45:46.369
He's the one that attacked me.

306
00:45:59.220 --> 00:46:02.123
We are here to make peace.

307
00:46:03.510 --> 00:46:05.628
Let your little thing mind himself.

308
00:46:06.962 --> 00:46:13.104
One to one, no problem...Six to one,
too much to ask of anyone.

309
00:46:13.914 --> 00:46:16.368
I see.

310
00:46:16.468 --> 00:46:18.984
Prepare for match!

311
00:46:21.976 --> 00:46:24.854
Whoa Mr. Han, does he want us to fight?

312
00:46:27.230 --> 00:46:30.669
We are not here to fight.

313
00:46:34.559 --> 00:46:38.301
You attack my students
and disrespect my studio?!

314
00:46:38.763 --> 00:46:42.230
You want to leave?
Not so easy.

315
00:46:43.502 --> 00:46:46.194
Master Li...

316
00:46:48.965 --> 00:46:51.118
You both came here.

317
00:46:51.734 --> 00:46:55.482
One of you fights now.

318
00:46:59.783 --> 00:47:03.655
The boy will fight there.

319
00:47:06.689 --> 00:47:09.516
OPEN KUNG FU TOURNAMENT

320
00:47:16.115 --> 00:47:19.660
We accept your challenge.

321
00:47:21.195 --> 00:47:26.467
Please instruct your students
to leave my boy alone to train.

322
00:47:28.023 --> 00:47:30.076
Attention!

323
00:47:32.758 --> 00:47:35.698
From now on the little thing
is to be left alone...

324
00:47:35.798 --> 00:47:37.791
until the tournament.

325
00:47:37.891 --> 00:47:40.927
- Understood?!
- Yes!

326
00:47:45.814 --> 00:47:50.086
If he does not show up
for the competition...

327
00:47:50.186 --> 00:47:55.028
I will bring pain to him and you.

328
00:48:05.704 --> 00:48:08.721
So, that go pretty much
how you planned it?

329
00:48:09.137 --> 00:48:10.955
There's good news and bad news.

330
00:48:11.055 --> 00:48:14.134
The good news is they promised
to leave you alone.

331
00:48:14.402 --> 00:48:18.158
- Really?
- While you prepare.

332
00:48:18.545 --> 00:48:21.047
Prepare for what?

333
00:48:21.066 --> 00:48:25.391
The tournament.
You'll fight them all, one by one.

334
00:48:26.177 --> 00:48:28.339
Huh?

335
00:48:29.558 --> 00:48:33.026
So the bad news is now
they get to beat me up in public.

336
00:48:33.210 --> 00:48:36.475
- Yes.
- Great. Thanks. Thanks a lot.

337
00:48:36.623 --> 00:48:39.339
They're gonna kill me.
You saw their Kung Fu.

338
00:48:39.757 --> 00:48:43.496
That's not Kung Fu. That does not
represent China.

339
00:48:43.541 --> 00:48:47.783
That bad man teach them really bad
things that hurt, a lot.

340
00:48:50.681 --> 00:48:55.302
More good news.
I will teach you real Kung Fu.

341
00:48:58.228 --> 00:49:00.075
Yes.

342
00:49:09.212 --> 00:49:14.091
- See you later, mom.
- Hey, wait. This is early for you for a Saturday.

343
00:49:14.191 --> 00:49:17.222
- Mr. Han will teach me Kung Fu.
- The maintenance man?

344
00:49:17.322 --> 00:49:19.734
It's China mom,
everybody knows Kung Fu.

345
00:49:19.787 --> 00:49:21.285
Dre, you know how do I feel about
your fighting.

346
00:49:21.320 --> 00:49:24.856
Kung Fu is not fight mom, it's about
making peace with your enemy.

347
00:49:24.891 --> 00:49:27.868
- Be careful, Dre.
- Yeah.

348
00:50:06.411 --> 00:50:08.692
Mr. Han?

349
00:50:30.122 --> 00:50:33.903
- Mr. Han?
- Back here.

350
00:50:36.238 --> 00:50:39.348
You know you have a car
in your living room, Mr. Han?

351
00:50:42.352 --> 00:50:46.719
Okay, I was thinking about yesterday. I know
I was kinda freaking out about the tournament...

352
00:50:46.819 --> 00:50:49.187
but I realized something last night.

353
00:50:49.340 --> 00:50:55.107
I'm an athlete. My number one asset
is I'm fast, okay?!

354
00:50:55.207 --> 00:50:59.533
I'm quick. I'm quick.
Got the speed. Cat speed.

355
00:51:00.207 --> 00:51:03.833
You see? I'm quick yeah, you see?
In the US, I used to take gymnastic at PAL,

356
00:51:03.834 --> 00:51:05.946
that's Police Athletic League, to check it,
right?

357
00:51:07.947 --> 00:51:10.463
Boom. You see that?

358
00:51:13.173 --> 00:51:17.314
My Uncle Reymi used to date that
Brazilian girl and he learned Jiu-Jitsu.

359
00:51:17.414 --> 00:51:20.430
And he taught some of it to me.
As like, locks and holds and stuff, it's okay.

360
00:51:20.530 --> 00:51:22.941
Attack me.

361
00:51:28.059 --> 00:51:31.089
You see that? Feel that?
I can break it.

362
00:51:31.124 --> 00:51:34.230
I'm choosing not to.
To press your luck. It's dangerous.

363
00:51:34.265 --> 00:51:37.021
And he also taught me Capoeira so...

364
00:51:37.061 --> 00:51:40.448
Can't touch me. Can't touch...

365
00:51:44.587 --> 00:51:47.256
Was that antique?

366
00:51:47.752 --> 00:51:51.591
Pick up your jacket.

367
00:51:53.484 --> 00:51:56.201
So basically Mr. Han,
what I'm trying to say is...

368
00:51:56.202 --> 00:51:59.901
I got a good foundation here.
You know, like I said. I'm just...

369
00:52:00.623 --> 00:52:03.617
Might not be as hard to teach me
as other people, you know.

370
00:52:03.791 --> 00:52:05.936
- Hang it up.
- Okay.

371
00:52:06.690 --> 00:52:11.241
- Happy now?
- Take it down.

372
00:52:13.350 --> 00:52:16.918
- You just...
- Take it down.

373
00:52:19.778 --> 00:52:21.901
Put it on.

374
00:52:26.814 --> 00:52:29.105
Take it off.

375
00:52:29.205 --> 00:52:31.321
- I already did all of this.
- Take it off.

376
00:52:31.421 --> 00:52:32.870
Can you just tell me,
why I'm doing this?

377
00:52:32.871 --> 00:52:34.870
Take it off.

378
00:52:37.903 --> 00:52:40.704
Hang it up.

379
00:52:43.887 --> 00:52:46.577
Take it down.

380
00:52:46.677 --> 00:52:49.156
Put it on the ground.

381
00:52:50.316 --> 00:52:52.853
Pick it up.

382
00:52:53.620 --> 00:52:55.191
Hang up.

383
00:52:55.978 --> 00:52:57.826
Take it down.

384
00:53:00.568 --> 00:53:03.018
Put it on.

385
00:53:03.356 --> 00:53:05.535
Take it off.

386
00:53:06.565 --> 00:53:08.853
Put it on the ground.

387
00:53:09.219 --> 00:53:11.391
Pick it up.

388
00:53:11.933 --> 00:53:14.279
Hang it up.

389
00:53:14.622 --> 00:53:19.323
Take it down.
Put it on.

390
00:53:19.985 --> 00:53:22.539
Take it off.

391
00:53:22.823 --> 00:53:25.855
Hang it up.

392
00:53:34.293 --> 00:53:39.142
Mr. Han, why do you have
a car in your living room?

393
00:53:39.242 --> 00:53:42.047
No street parking.

394
00:53:49.043 --> 00:53:51.300
Hey!

395
00:53:52.301 --> 00:53:55.619
So how did it go?
What you learned?

396
00:53:55.793 --> 00:53:58.463
Nothing.

397
00:54:33.221 --> 00:54:36.094
Uniform on Uniform day.

398
00:54:36.129 --> 00:54:40.975
- You're fighting in the tournament?
- Yeah, how did you hear?

399
00:54:41.107 --> 00:54:42.852
Everybody knows.

400
00:54:45.485 --> 00:54:51.834
- I hope you have a good teacher.
- Yeah, me too.

401
00:54:52.000 --> 00:54:54.300
He's a maintenance man.

402
00:54:54.656 --> 00:54:56.918
- Can I ask you a question?
- Yes.

403
00:54:57.652 --> 00:55:03.366
Well, I know you're practicing, and I think I'm practicing, I mean,
I don't know what I'm doing...

404
00:55:03.401 --> 00:55:09.768
- But, we both kind of practicing, you know and...
- Are you going to that Shi-Shi festival?

405
00:55:09.948 --> 00:55:15.770
Yeah, I mean, I've missed
the Shi-Di Festival since I've been in China.

406
00:55:18.307 --> 00:55:24.183
- Go to the Shaolin theater.
- Okay. You want me to meet you?

407
00:55:25.115 --> 00:55:31.237
Oh, oh, so like Shaolin theater, okay Shi-Fi-Shi festival.
Shaolin theater, okay. Cool.

408
00:55:33.172 --> 00:55:36.190
- When is it again?
- Tomorrow. The show starts at seven.

409
00:55:36.347 --> 00:55:41.588
Okay. So tomorrow, Shaolin theater.
Shi-Shi festival at seven.

410
00:55:41.688 --> 00:55:44.610
- See you tomorrow.
- Shi-Shi festival.

411
00:55:44.710 --> 00:55:48.318
- Festival. - Shi-Shi festival.
- Okay. - Okay.

412
00:56:10.707 --> 00:56:12.429
Mr. Han?

413
00:56:12.727 --> 00:56:17.119
- Mr. Han, can I come in?
- You may come in.

414
00:56:22.549 --> 00:56:24.318
Where's your jacket?

415
00:56:25.968 --> 00:56:29.768
- I thought, I was warmin' up without it.
- Go get it.

416
00:56:29.849 --> 00:56:32.043
You want me to go
all way back, just to get it?

417
00:56:32.143 --> 00:56:35.357
Yes, all the way back
where you hide it.

418
00:57:01.266 --> 00:57:05.721
- This is not right.
- What? I'm doing it.

419
00:57:07.843 --> 00:57:10.115
No.

420
00:57:10.205 --> 00:57:12.407
- Something is missing.
- Nothing is missing.

421
00:57:21.016 --> 00:57:24.711
You forgot, this.

422
00:57:25.828 --> 00:57:27.637
Attitude.

423
00:57:28.816 --> 00:57:30.978
Shake it off.

424
00:57:34.780 --> 00:57:39.637
Attitude.
Yes, that's it.

425
00:57:39.737 --> 00:57:44.037
Okay, Mr. Han. I get it. I'm sorry.
I shouldn't have treated my mom like that.

426
00:57:44.072 --> 00:57:45.629
You're right.

427
00:57:49.207 --> 00:57:53.608
- Put it on the ground.
- Hello.

428
00:57:54.340 --> 00:57:58.459
Ow, hey mom.
Um, did you get the tickets?

429
00:57:58.781 --> 00:58:04.763
Yes, I got the tickets,
and I got an extra one for Mr. Han.

430
00:58:04.929 --> 00:58:08.661
- But I didn't say...
- Dre, stop it.

431
00:58:08.738 --> 00:58:12.456
Mr. Han, would you like to go with us
to the Shi-Shi festival?

432
00:58:12.556 --> 00:58:15.757
No, thank you.
Too many people.

433
00:58:15.800 --> 00:58:20.099
- Yeah, mom. Way too many people.
- Yeah, but I already bought the tickets.

434
00:58:20.199 --> 00:58:22.965
- I don't go...
- Mr. Han, I'm not taking "no" for an answer.

435
00:58:23.065 --> 00:58:25.899
You'll have fun. You need
to get out the house, okay?

436
00:58:25.999 --> 00:58:29.509
Here are your clothes, Dre.
Come on, hurry up and change.

437
00:58:33.599 --> 00:58:34.509
Dre...

438
00:58:35.721 --> 00:58:38.889
Pick up your jacket!

439
00:58:50.485 --> 00:58:54.789
You were right Mr. Han,
there are a lot of people here.

440
00:58:54.790 --> 00:58:56.789
Chinese Valentine's Day.

441
00:59:10.620 --> 00:59:15.637
Yeah, Mom. I'm going to go get something
to eat, then going to go to the bathroom.

442
00:59:15.672 --> 00:59:17.919
Be back, right here,
in 20 minutes.

443
00:59:19.836 --> 00:59:22.971
- I love you.
- I love you, too. Be careful. 20 minutes.

444
00:59:23.071 --> 00:59:26.037
- 20.
- Okay.

445
01:00:19.037 --> 01:00:21.364
I got this, and this for you.

446
01:00:21.464 --> 01:00:26.193
I downloaded this.
It has a very cool violins stuff, and I...

447
01:00:26.293 --> 01:00:30.384
I thought maybe you could play along and...
It's not like Bach and...

448
01:00:30.385 --> 01:00:33.784
but, I thought maybe
you'd like it and...

449
01:00:59.369 --> 01:01:04.868
- So, um, do you have any kids?
- No.

450
01:01:06.519 --> 01:01:09.231
Oh, how's Dre doing?

451
01:01:09.467 --> 01:01:13.398
- Um, Shao Dre making a progress.
- Shao Dre?

452
01:01:13.433 --> 01:01:16.503
Yes, Chinese pollito.

453
01:01:18.429 --> 01:01:21.417
So, um, how many students do you have?

454
01:01:22.496 --> 01:01:25.011
- Including Shao Dre?
- Yeah.

455
01:01:25.916 --> 01:01:28.038
One.

456
01:01:34.249 --> 01:01:36.804
So, what's the show about?

457
01:01:38.863 --> 01:01:41.496
It's the story of the Goddess...

458
01:01:41.575 --> 01:01:44.130
and a boy she loves.

459
01:01:44.366 --> 01:01:47.944
I love this story.

460
01:01:49.651 --> 01:01:53.071
Her mother does not approve of him.

461
01:01:53.150 --> 01:02:00.500
So, she cuts a wide river in the sky
to separate them forever.

462
01:02:00.540 --> 01:02:05.139
But once a year,
all the birds in the sky...

463
01:02:05.678 --> 01:02:10.592
felt sad for them,
and they form a bridge.

464
01:02:11.889 --> 01:02:19.293
So the two of them may be
together for a single night.

465
01:02:26.038 --> 01:02:29.932
I'll be there at you audition,
if you come to my tournament.

466
01:02:30.541 --> 01:02:34.076
- Okay, I'll be there.
- Pinky swear.

467
01:02:35.432 --> 01:02:37.978
See, you wrap your hands like this.

468
01:02:38.417 --> 01:02:43.502
I swear that I'll be there at your audition,
no matter what happens.

469
01:02:43.602 --> 01:02:49.071
And I promise to cheer bigger
than anyone else when you win.

470
01:03:26.853 --> 01:03:29.133
What up, Mr. Han?

471
01:03:30.352 --> 01:03:32.789
Did I say come in?

472
01:03:32.946 --> 01:03:36.091
Um, I think you did. I mean...

473
01:03:40.595 --> 01:03:44.251
- Mr. Han, can I please come in?
- Yes.

474
01:03:46.816 --> 01:03:50.674
- So, what we are doing today?
- Same.

475
01:04:38.573 --> 01:04:44.814
Mr. Han, I told you. I get it, okay?
Be respectful! I got it!

476
01:04:45.408 --> 01:04:50.193
I put my jacket on a thousand times,
and I took it off a thousand times, okay?

477
01:04:50.250 --> 01:04:52.952
This is stupid. I'm done!

478
01:04:52.987 --> 01:04:55.671
Let them beat me up,
if they want to.

479
01:04:56.681 --> 01:05:01.297
You know why you only have
one student? 'Cause you don't know Kung Fu.

480
01:05:01.348 --> 01:05:04.807
- Shao Dre!
- What?

481
01:05:09.838 --> 01:05:12.197
Come here.

482
01:05:20.013 --> 01:05:23.787
- Jacket on!
- Mr. Han, I already...- Jacket on!

483
01:05:33.359 --> 01:05:37.782
- Jacket on!
- I don't have a jacket...- Jacket on!

484
01:05:44.792 --> 01:05:47.164
Be strong.

485
01:05:47.199 --> 01:05:49.644
Jacket on.

486
01:05:50.056 --> 01:05:52.709
Firm.

487
01:05:53.319 --> 01:05:55.522
Jacket off.

488
01:05:56.957 --> 01:05:58.953
Remember...

489
01:05:59.053 --> 01:06:03.808
always strong...
Jacket off.

490
01:06:07.621 --> 01:06:09.644
Strong.

491
01:06:10.445 --> 01:06:13.236
Left foot back.
Right foot back.

492
01:06:13.354 --> 01:06:15.595
Left foot back.
Pick up your jacket!

493
01:06:17.206 --> 01:06:20.115
- Whoa, Mr. ...- Focus!
- Okay. - Always concentrate.

494
01:06:20.352 --> 01:06:24.726
Left back. Right foot back.
Pick up your jacket!

495
01:06:24.865 --> 01:06:27.428
Stay.

496
01:06:29.181 --> 01:06:31.851
Pick up your jacket.

497
01:06:35.571 --> 01:06:37.091
Strong.

498
01:06:37.191 --> 01:06:38.959
Hang it up.

499
01:06:39.191 --> 01:06:40.959
Hang it up.

500
01:06:42.043 --> 01:06:44.414
And attitude!

501
01:06:45.010 --> 01:06:47.147
Strike!

502
01:06:47.148 --> 01:06:49.602
Hang up and attitude!

503
01:06:49.603 --> 01:06:52.683
Harder.
Harder.

504
01:06:55.108 --> 01:06:59.038
Good, but no face.

505
01:06:59.510 --> 01:07:01.593
Jacket off!

506
01:07:23.559 --> 01:07:27.491
Kung Fu lives in everything
we do, Shao Dre.

507
01:07:27.844 --> 01:07:32.758
It lives in how we put on a jacket,
and how we take off the jacket.

508
01:07:33.112 --> 01:07:36.178
It lives in
how we treat people.

509
01:07:37.869 --> 01:07:43.105
Everything is Kung Fu.

510
01:08:26.246 --> 01:08:32.103
- So, why do not we take the Shiroko?
- I don't drive the Shiroko.

511
01:08:32.615 --> 01:08:38.395
- Do you have a license?
- Yes.

512
01:08:38.592 --> 01:08:44.213
So you have a license and a car
and we're in the train?

513
01:08:45.248 --> 01:08:48.753
- Please, be quiet.
- I'm just sayin'...

514
01:08:48.788 --> 01:08:52.798
seems like we could've saved
a lot of money, don't you think?

515
01:08:54.341 --> 01:08:59.687
- Do you always ask these many questions?
- I'm sorry.

516
01:09:00.670 --> 01:09:03.461
So, what we are learning today?

517
01:09:04.877 --> 01:09:07.235
Chi.

518
01:09:07.786 --> 01:09:14.236
Eternal Energy.
The essence of life.

519
01:09:14.771 --> 01:09:18.706
It moves inside of us,
flows through our bodies.

520
01:09:18.741 --> 01:09:21.859
Give us power from within.

521
01:09:26.532 --> 01:09:30.346
I get it,
like the "Force" from Star Wars.

522
01:09:30.856 --> 01:09:35.921
You're Yoda,
and I'm like... I'm like a Jedi.

523
01:10:08.302 --> 01:10:11.919
- Is this where you learned Kung Fu?
- Yes.

524
01:10:13.884 --> 01:10:16.360
Everything good about me
was born here.

525
01:10:16.951 --> 01:10:20.756
So Dre, you gotta leave your backpack
and skateboard here.

526
01:10:20.791 --> 01:10:24.262
- So, where are we going?
- The journey to the top of the mountain.

527
01:10:24.301 --> 01:10:27.053
Tomb of the Dragon Well.

528
01:10:29.413 --> 01:10:35.359
Dragon Well? It's probably,
closer than it is, I'm looking at it.

529
01:10:36.386 --> 01:10:38.890
Right?

530
01:11:06.373 --> 01:11:10.264
- Are we there yet?
- Soon.

531
01:11:12.631 --> 01:11:16.285
- How do you say water in Chinese?
- Shui.

532
01:11:16.555 --> 01:11:19.071
I need some shui.

533
01:11:19.471 --> 01:11:23.553
I'm really thirsty.

534
01:11:26.994 --> 01:11:31.947
- I'm thirsty, Mr. Han.
- Water on top of the mountain.

535
01:13:49.604 --> 01:13:52.080
Shao Dre.

536
01:14:00.886 --> 01:14:03.755
The journey is complete.

537
01:14:06.022 --> 01:14:11.717
- This is the Dragon Well?
- Yes.

538
01:14:16.276 --> 01:14:21.387
I stood here with my father,
when I was your age.

539
01:14:21.544 --> 01:14:26.261
He told me that's the magic
Kung Fu water.

540
01:14:34.965 --> 01:14:39.100
You drink and nothing
can defeat you.

541
01:14:49.961 --> 01:14:53.930
It's the best water I've ever tasted.

542
01:14:55.626 --> 01:14:59.344
- Did you see the lady with the snake?
- Yes.

543
01:14:59.488 --> 01:15:02.076
She was doing the Cobra thing.
She was like...

544
01:15:02.240 --> 01:15:06.282
copying the snake. And it was like...
right here, and she was like...

545
01:15:08.126 --> 01:15:11.762
You did not watch closely enough,
Shao Dre.

546
01:15:12.082 --> 01:15:14.965
The snake was copying the woman.

547
01:15:15.318 --> 01:15:19.013
What? I don't get it.

548
01:15:27.737 --> 01:15:29.332
Look.

549
01:15:29.367 --> 01:15:35.764
- What do you see?
- Me, well my reflection. - Yes.

550
01:15:37.774 --> 01:15:42.066
- Now, what do you see?
- It's blurry. - Yes.

551
01:15:42.166 --> 01:15:47.287
That woman was sliced through water
quiet and calm.

552
01:15:47.404 --> 01:15:50.118
In here and in here.

553
01:15:50.921 --> 01:15:56.696
So, the snake reflects her action,
like still water.

554
01:15:56.944 --> 01:15:59.448
- Like a mirror?
- Yes.

555
01:16:01.287 --> 01:16:04.872
So, she controlled a snake
by doing nothing?

556
01:16:07.166 --> 01:16:12.198
Being still and doing nothing,
are two very different things.

557
01:16:15.736 --> 01:16:19.116
- She used her Chi on that snake, didn't she?
- Very good.

558
01:16:19.234 --> 01:16:22.847
You gotta teach me that.
How to control people.

559
01:16:23.021 --> 01:16:27.392
There is only one person
you need to learn how to control.

560
01:16:30.639 --> 01:16:33.155
Who?

561
01:16:33.190 --> 01:16:37.321
Empty your mind.
Flow with my movement.

562
01:16:37.435 --> 01:16:40.294
Connect to the energy,
around you.

563
01:16:40.453 --> 01:16:45.328
- I kinda just want to learn the cobra thing.
- Cobra takes a lifetime.

564
01:16:45.367 --> 01:16:49.023
- Requires great focus.
- But I have great focus?!

565
01:16:52.645 --> 01:16:55.706
- Oh my God. Mr. Han...
- Your focus,

566
01:16:55.741 --> 01:16:59.810
- needs more focus.
- Mr. Han...

567
01:17:38.141 --> 01:17:40.810
Thank you, Mr. Han.

568
01:18:01.780 --> 01:18:05.504
There's no such thing
as fortune cookies in China.

569
01:18:05.739 --> 01:18:08.216
Dre, please be careful
crossing the street.

570
01:18:08.334 --> 01:18:14.798
You just scared the life out of me,
the other day. They have the "right-of-way".

571
01:18:17.799 --> 01:18:20.187
And the symbols. I can't get
the symbols right on the bathrooms.

572
01:18:20.594 --> 01:18:23.187
And I'm still walkin' into the men's restroom.

573
01:18:23.287 --> 01:18:26.232
The other day I walked in,
there was this 90 years old Chinese man,

574
01:18:26.287 --> 01:18:28.232
he thought he was getting a little treat.

575
01:18:28.267 --> 01:18:32.247
Dre, please stop that! You look crazy!
Here, eat your noodles!

576
01:18:55.633 --> 01:18:58.670
Mr. Han,
what's goin' on?

577
01:19:00.676 --> 01:19:02.837
Anticipation.

578
01:19:03.544 --> 01:19:05.196
I can't see...

579
01:19:05.274 --> 01:19:07.437
Don't see it, feel it.

580
01:19:07.711 --> 01:19:09.520
Dammit, Mr. Han!

581
01:19:09.991 --> 01:19:12.231
I felt that one!

582
01:19:15.016 --> 01:19:17.703
- Mr. Han.
- What?

583
01:19:23.032 --> 01:19:27.243
- Concentrate, okay?
- Okay. Do I get the stick now?

584
01:19:48.782 --> 01:19:51.794
- Dre, you okay?
- I'm okay.

585
01:19:55.614 --> 01:19:58.700
What's up Mr. Han, what time
we are trainin' tomorrow?

586
01:19:58.735 --> 01:20:01.786
Shao Dre, we are not training tomorrow.

587
01:20:01.943 --> 01:20:03.476
Why not?

588
01:20:05.481 --> 01:20:07.878
- Wu chi pi fan
- Wu chi pi fan?

589
01:20:07.879 --> 01:20:11.141
It means: "Too much of something
is not good."

590
01:20:11.259 --> 01:20:13.776
You train a lot, you need to rest.

591
01:20:13.894 --> 01:20:18.403
A day off?
Yes, Mr. Han! Yes!

592
01:20:18.812 --> 01:20:22.083
Shao Dre needs to rest.
Yes, Mr. Han.

593
01:20:23.123 --> 01:20:28.316
You rest, too.
I love you, Mr. Han. Peace!

594
01:20:45.262 --> 01:20:47.146
Are you okay?

595
01:20:47.246 --> 01:20:51.808
- My audition is tomorrow at a six.
- Isn't it what you've been practicing for?

596
01:20:51.887 --> 01:20:56.664
- Yes, of course.
- Don't worry, you got it.

597
01:20:56.854 --> 01:20:59.922
What if they don't pick me?

598
01:21:02.264 --> 01:21:04.156
Meiying, wait!

599
01:21:05.629 --> 01:21:07.779
First of all,
I'm going to be there with you.

600
01:21:07.879 --> 01:21:12.119
And B, all you have to do is what your
teacher says. Play the pauses.

601
01:21:12.219 --> 01:21:14.497
It's easy, watch.

602
01:21:16.490 --> 01:21:18.223
You see?

603
01:21:19.679 --> 01:21:24.108
- I have to practice.
- Wait.

604
01:21:24.109 --> 01:21:25.638
Wu gi bi fan.

605
01:21:25.639 --> 01:21:26.736
What?

606
01:21:26.739 --> 01:21:28.736
I'm sorry,
I don't think you don't speak Chinese.

607
01:21:28.737 --> 01:21:34.315
Wu gi bi fan.
Too much of good stuff is a bad stuff?

608
01:21:34.316 --> 01:21:36.633
Ow...Wu chi pi fan.

609
01:21:36.634 --> 01:21:39.819
Yeah.
Wu gi bi FUN.

610
01:21:41.234 --> 01:21:43.570
- Come on.
- Where are we going?

611
01:21:43.766 --> 01:21:46.658
Have you ever been to the gym?
C'mon, we are going to have some fun.

612
01:21:47.319 --> 01:21:50.672
Come on, I know you want
to go have some fun!

613
01:22:18.662 --> 01:22:22.297
Okay, that's going to give you
some serious gas.

614
01:22:36.573 --> 01:22:39.442
- What do you see?
- Me.

615
01:22:39.993 --> 01:22:43.806
- Now, what do you see?
- Me.

616
01:23:13.917 --> 01:23:14.596
Go, come on.

617
01:23:14.597 --> 01:23:18.596
<i>You're dancing machine.
That was pretty good!<i/></i>

618
01:23:20.643 --> 01:23:24.532
<i>Here comes, round two.<i/></i>

619
01:24:15.643 --> 01:24:17.532
<i>You're hot.<i/></i>

620
01:24:22.677 --> 01:24:27.717
-That's like American dancing.
Like, you should have a group. -No.

621
01:24:27.835 --> 01:24:33.573
With like, other people in it
dancing behind you, doin' the same stuff.

622
01:24:45.323 --> 01:24:49.141
- The audition, it was changed to today.
- But they said, it's tomorrow.

623
01:24:49.241 --> 01:24:51.979
Something happened.
It is in 20 minutes.

624
01:24:52.120 --> 01:24:55.463
My father is coming to get me.

625
01:27:57.575 --> 01:28:01.782
Hey, she's like totally going to get it, right,
because that was just great.

626
01:28:36.165 --> 01:28:39.499
Hey! That was fantastic.

627
01:28:39.534 --> 01:28:43.220
That was... You just...
You played so beautifully, and...

628
01:28:44.364 --> 01:28:46.811
We can no longer be friends.

629
01:28:47.572 --> 01:28:50.980
You are bad for my life.

630
01:29:03.643 --> 01:29:06.516
See you at the tournament.

631
01:29:07.097 --> 01:29:10.215
Don't be late for that.

632
01:29:54.879 --> 01:29:57.396
Mr. Han!
Mr. Han!

633
01:30:02.941 --> 01:30:05.463
We'll not train today.

634
01:30:20.391 --> 01:30:26.181
- What are you doing?
- It's July 8th.

635
01:31:37.478 --> 01:31:40.559
Why did you wreck the car?

636
01:31:58.798 --> 01:32:01.943
His name was Kang Kang.

637
01:32:02.219 --> 01:32:05.953
Shao Dre, how old are you?

638
01:32:05.988 --> 01:32:08.272
Twelve.

639
01:32:08.430 --> 01:32:11.142
He was ten.

640
01:32:12.360 --> 01:32:15.388
He was so beautiful.

641
01:32:17.667 --> 01:32:21.226
Her name was Xiang.

642
01:32:21.974 --> 01:32:25.475
She was a singer.

643
01:32:27.761 --> 01:32:31.101
Not professional.

644
01:32:32.330 --> 01:32:35.545
She sang only for me.

645
01:33:12.881 --> 01:33:15.396
What happened?

646
01:33:23.259 --> 01:33:26.247
There was a steep hill.

647
01:33:26.482 --> 01:33:29.391
Lots of rain.

648
01:33:30.138 --> 01:33:34.442
The car, it just...

649
01:33:35.254 --> 01:33:38.226
I was driving.

650
01:33:38.350 --> 01:33:41.741
We argued about something.

651
01:33:43.155 --> 01:33:45.200
I was so angry.

652
01:33:45.672 --> 01:33:48.031
I lost control.

653
01:33:48.542 --> 01:33:52.158
I try to remember...

654
01:33:52.198 --> 01:33:55.381
but I can not remember what we're
argued about.

655
01:33:56.678 --> 01:34:00.020
I hope it was something important.

656
01:34:03.181 --> 01:34:07.606
Every year, I fix the car.

657
01:34:08.602 --> 01:34:12.427
But still fix nothing.

658
01:39:02.202 --> 01:39:04.427
Mr. Han!

659
01:40:55.331 --> 01:41:01.665
Win or lose, doesn't matter.
Fight hard.

660
01:41:02.810 --> 01:41:06.662
Earn respect.
The boys leave you alone.

661
01:41:10.436 --> 01:41:13.345
I have a present for you.

662
01:41:18.579 --> 01:41:20.308
Oh! Mr. Han.

663
01:41:21.802 --> 01:41:24.043
This is the one Bruce Lee had.

664
01:41:24.161 --> 01:41:26.205
Great.

665
01:41:26.519 --> 01:41:28.917
Thank you.

666
01:41:31.786 --> 01:41:35.873
You have taught me
a very important lesson, Shao Dre.

667
01:41:37.236 --> 01:41:45.615
Life will knock us down, but we can
choose, whether or not,  to get back up.

668
01:41:48.059 --> 01:41:51.867
You're the best friend
I've ever had, Mr. Han.

669
01:42:08.761 --> 01:42:11.865
Okay.

670
01:42:14.521 --> 01:42:18.151
Wait!
Can you help me with something?

671
01:42:22.683 --> 01:42:24.256
Dre?

672
01:42:24.413 --> 01:42:28.030
Is your dad home?

673
01:42:31.638 --> 01:42:32.833
Sir...

674
01:42:33.690 --> 01:42:36.395
My name is Dre Parker.

675
01:42:36.520 --> 01:42:43.783
My actions have brought
dishonor to your family.

676
01:42:44.085 --> 01:42:49.003
Your daughter has been
a great friend to me.

677
01:42:49.206 --> 01:42:52.247
And from her I have learned...

678
01:42:52.889 --> 01:42:55.135
...that a true friend...

679
01:42:55.235 --> 01:42:58.317
...is a person
who makes your life better.

680
01:42:58.496 --> 01:43:03.271
But, if you give me a second chance...

681
01:43:03.557 --> 01:43:07.263
...I promise that I will be...

682
01:43:07.363 --> 01:43:14.981
...the best friend your
daughter has ever had.

683
01:43:18.290 --> 01:43:21.159
That's it.

684
01:43:35.633 --> 01:43:41.165
My daughter told me that she made
a promise to be at your tournament.

685
01:43:41.441 --> 01:43:45.803
In our family,
we do not break our promises.

686
01:43:49.141 --> 01:43:51.040
Good luck!

687
01:43:53.041 --> 01:43:54.800
Thank you.

688
01:44:01.985 --> 01:44:04.511
Rock and roll.

689
01:44:28.573 --> 01:44:32.473
Let the tournament begin!

690
01:45:05.067 --> 01:45:07.639
Shao Dre, you're up.

691
01:45:09.338 --> 01:45:11.660
- What's that?
- The rule book.

692
01:45:12.268 --> 01:45:15.869
- You don't know the rules?
- Of course I know the rules, it's simple.

693
01:45:15.870 --> 01:45:18.105
You hit him,
and don't let him hit you.

694
01:45:18.243 --> 01:45:19.911
What?

695
01:45:20.128 --> 01:45:22.675
Mr. Han, they're going to kill me.

696
01:45:24.372 --> 01:45:30.544
Two points to win. Win it two times.
Go. Focus. Focus.

697
01:46:00.441 --> 01:46:02.573
That's a warning.
You cannot run off the mat.

698
01:46:02.673 --> 01:46:05.727
Next time you lose a point.
Go.

699
01:46:05.772 --> 01:46:09.052
- Be strong.
- Come on, Dre.

700
01:46:43.544 --> 01:46:46.892
- Good job. Next time, no face.
- I'm sorry, I can't help it.

701
01:46:46.985 --> 01:46:49.250
The next point winner.

702
01:46:49.255 --> 01:46:51.325
Come on, baby.

703
01:49:39.009 --> 01:49:43.334
Dre Parker advances to the semi-finals!

704
01:49:44.088 --> 01:49:48.000
From now on, the semi-final matches,
three points to win.

705
01:49:48.100 --> 01:49:49.984
Be kinda hot if I
won this thing, huh, Mr. Han?

706
01:49:50.102 --> 01:49:55.327
- Be kinda hot if you focused.
- Yeah, well, after that.

707
01:50:03.553 --> 01:50:08.322
<i>And now the 1st semi-final
of the evening.</i>

708
01:50:08.411 --> 01:50:09.911
TOURNAMENT OF CHAMPIONS
SEMI-FINAL

709
01:50:10.523 --> 01:50:12.552
First round:
Cheng Vs. Wu Ping.

710
01:51:50.812 --> 01:51:54.260
Cheng advances to final.

711
01:52:07.220 --> 01:52:11.688
Next semi-final:
Introducing Fighting Dragon Liang...

712
01:52:13.264 --> 01:52:18.004
...and the surprising finalist, Dre Parker.

713
01:52:25.769 --> 01:52:29.346
Empty your mind. Focus.

714
01:53:27.205 --> 01:53:30.581
You're disqualified!

715
01:53:36.854 --> 01:53:39.265
Are you okay?

716
01:53:54.642 --> 01:53:57.436
He's done.

717
01:53:57.536 --> 01:54:03.332
I'm sorry, you should not continue.
You've brought honor to your family.

718
01:54:05.125 --> 01:54:09.298
The doctor says, you did great.

719
01:54:18.615 --> 01:54:23.065
- You okay, baby?
- Yeah, I'm okay.

720
01:54:24.940 --> 01:54:28.148
Dre Parker has 2 minutes to
return to the match.

721
01:54:28.248 --> 01:54:30.973
If he's unable to return...

722
01:54:31.073 --> 01:54:35.630
...the Fighting Dragons
win by default.

723
01:54:37.082 --> 01:54:39.753
Can you guys give us a second?

724
01:54:40.724 --> 01:54:46.316
Yeah, okay. Sure baby,
whatever you need.

725
01:54:53.633 --> 01:54:56.542
Do you think I could have won?

726
01:54:56.974 --> 01:54:59.923
Win or lose doesn't matter,
Shao Dre.

727
01:55:00.788 --> 01:55:03.540
You know that's not what I mean.

728
01:55:07.078 --> 01:55:12.345
Yes, I think you had a good chance.

729
01:55:14.398 --> 01:55:17.828
So, let's do the fiery cup thing.

730
01:55:19.980 --> 01:55:25.105
You don't need to fight anymore.
You have proven everything you need to prove.

731
01:55:25.205 --> 01:55:28.624
What, that I can get
beat up easy, and then quit?

732
01:55:28.761 --> 01:55:31.655
That's not balance,
that's not real Kung Fu.

733
01:55:31.896 --> 01:55:37.754
You said, when life knocks you down,
you could choose whether or not to get back up.

734
01:55:37.927 --> 01:55:42.102
Well, I'm tryin' to get back up.
And why won't you help me?

735
01:55:44.537 --> 01:55:46.193
Because...

736
01:55:46.311 --> 01:55:50.478
I cannot watch you
get hurt anymore.

737
01:55:53.286 --> 01:55:57.742
Please, Mr. Han. Please.

738
01:55:58.686 --> 01:56:05.106
Just tell me, Shao Dre. Why?
Why you need to go back out there so badly?

739
01:56:06.752 --> 01:56:10.408
Because I'm still scared.

740
01:56:13.197 --> 01:56:17.665
No matter what happens tonight
when I leave...

741
01:56:18.054 --> 01:56:21.278
...I don't want to be scared anymore.

742
01:56:32.566 --> 01:56:38.799
Since Dre Parker has
not returned to the ring...

743
01:56:57.545 --> 01:57:02.056
Dre Parker will fight!

744
01:58:53.652 --> 01:58:56.042
Shao Dre?

745
01:59:12.349 --> 01:59:15.455
Come on, Dre.
You can do this, Dre.

746
02:00:54.208 --> 02:00:57.499
- You okay?
- Yes, I'm okay.

747
02:01:00.162 --> 02:01:03.715
No mercy.

748
02:02:12.054 --> 02:02:17.208
The score is tied.
The next point wins!

749
02:05:08.013 --> 02:05:11.924
I'm so proud of you.

750
02:05:53.013 --> 02:06:04.924
